<title>GERMANY: BHF-Bank exercises ProSieben greenshoe.</title>
<headline>BHF-Bank exercises ProSieben greenshoe.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>BHF-Bank, the global coordinator for German television group ProSieben's initial public offering, said on Tuesday it had exercised the full greenshoe option for the share issue.</p>
<p>The greenshoe option, of 1.75 million preference shares, allows additional shares to be distributed to investors. The ProSieben listing was many times oversubscribed, meaning many would-be investors were not allocated shares.</p>
<p>BHF-Bank said a total of 17.5 million preference shares had now been placed. This equates to 50 percent of the company's basic capital.</p>
<p>ProSieben shares ended Monday's trade up 25 pfennigs at 90 marks. They listed on the market at 87 marks.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
